Same interpreter shape: parse builds nested operation lists and execute runs them by recursion (a loop runs its own list while the current cell is not zero), with the reference's tape (one cell, growing by one). The reference's Vec<Op> with Loop(Vec<Op>) is a list of nodes linked by next, a loop's body being the head of another list, stored in arrays (the language has no variable-length nested vectors); parse and execute recurse as in the reference (depth is the program's loop nesting, 7 here, within the language's 64-deep limit). The reference's u8 wrapping is masking; the text is read byte by byte from the request input. Other stores are checked and undo-logged. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: src, op, nxt, body, tape) is declared `unlogged`, kept out of the undo log.
